2026-11-08T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2486) 'Tri2d cli shared algorithm repo
 # uuid: ff7748c9-16e7-57be-82e3-0323b81ccffe
 # tags: rfd:title
 RFD:Prediscussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-11-08T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2486) 'A validated 2D constrained-Delaunay triangulation already backs a Python dataset pipeline and a godot-sandbox guest. Which repo should carry it?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2486) 'tri2d_cli wraps Geogram's real CDT2d behind a JSON stdin/stdout contract. GarmentCodeData v2's orig_lens pipeline (Python, replacing CGAL) shells out to it, and the sketch-mesh guest ported the same call sequence into its own curvenet guest as a native function.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2486) 'Check that the new repo exists, builds standalone with plain cmake . && make, and that neither GarmentCodeData nor the sketch-mesh guest vendors its own copy of the CLI source.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2486) 'Tri2d cli shared algorithm repo
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2486) 'See DETAILS.md for the full argument.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2486) 'See DETAILS.md for the full argument.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2486) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2486) 'Where does a triangulation two unrelated consumers share live?
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2486) 'Context and problem statement
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2486) 'tri2d_cli existed only as scratch files on two machines, this Mac's local port and the Windows desk's build, never committed to a repo. It wraps Geogram's real CDT2d (constrained Delaunay triangulation with hole removal) behind a small JSON-over-stdin/stdout CLI, validated against a known-area control case (see confirmation below).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2486) 'It has two independent consumers. GarmentCodeData v2's orig_lens regeneration pipeline (Python) shells out to the built binary in place of CGAL. The sketch-mesh repo's curvenet godot-sandbox guest ported the same point-flattening, constraint-insertion and hole-removal sequence into C++ as a native guest function, vmcall-verified on the Windows desk, reading native float vectors instead of JSON. Each consumer's repo serves a different domain from the algorithm itself.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2486) 'Decision drivers
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2486) '- The validation is the control case checked in confirmation. It should be proven once, in one repo, not re-proven inside each consumer.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2486) '- GarmentCodeData is a Python dataset-generation repo. Its only other caller is a Godot guest ELF, so a C++ triangulation library sits outside its domain.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2486) '- The sketch-mesh repo is a godot-sandbox guest repo. The standalone-CLI build path (cmake . && make, JSON-over-stdio) serves only the Python side, so it sits outside that repo's domain too.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2486) '- The vendored Geogram subset (BSD-3-Clause, Inria) needs to stay distinct from our own MIT code wherever it lands. Vendoring it twice doubles the licensing surface for no benefit.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2486) 'Considered options
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2486) '- Commit tri2d_cli into GarmentCodeData's own repo, and have the sketch-mesh guest re-derive its native function from scratch each time it drifts.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2486) '- Commit the CLI into the sketch-mesh repo and have GarmentCodeData's pipeline depend on that repo as a submodule.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2486) '- Place it as its own repo: the validated CLI, its vendored geogram-subset subtree, and the control test, with both consumers treating it as an external, versioned tool.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2486) 'Decision outcome
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2486) 'Chosen option: its own new repo. The algorithm and its validation belong to neither consumer, and a shared repo lets both read the same validated source instead of two copies drifting apart.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2486) 'The new repo carries:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2486) '- tri2d_cli.cpp and boolean_expression.cpp (MIT, ours).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2486) '- a vendored geogram-subset tree (Geogram 1.9.9, BSD-3-Clause, Inria), with its own LICENSE and CITATION.cff kept inside that subtree.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2486) '- A CMakeLists.txt that builds standalone with plain cmake . && make, no GarmentCode or Windows-desk directory assumptions.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2486) '- A README stating the JSON contract and the control case from confirmation as its smoke test.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2486) 'GarmentCodeData's pipeline and the sketch-mesh guest keep their own ports of the call sequence, a Python subprocess call and a native C++ guest function. This repo is where the algorithm itself is proven once.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2486) 'Consequences
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2486) '- Good: one validated triangulation, read by two consumers, instead of two copies that can silently diverge.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2486) '- Good: the BSD-3-Clause vendor subtree is licensed once, correctly scoped, instead of twice.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2486) '- Good: GarmentCodeData and the sketch-mesh guest each stay focused on their own domain. Neither carries the other's build path.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2486) '- Bad: a third consumer, or a fix found in one port, still has to be manually checked against this repo's tri2d_cli.cpp. The guest's C++ port is a separate translation, not a build dependency on this repo.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2486) 'Confirmation
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2486) '- The new repo exists, public, MIT-licensed for its own code, with the vendored geogram-subset tree kept under Geogram's BSD-3-Clause.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2486) '- cmake . && make on a clean macOS or Linux checkout builds tri2d_cli with no other directories present.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2486) '- The control case: a 10x10 square boundary, a 2x2 hole, and 2 interior points, piped into the built binary, sums to area 96.0, with no triangle centroid landing inside the hole.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-2486) 'More information
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-08T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-2486) 'Relates to the sketch-mesh repo's guest port of this same call sequence, and to GarmentCodeData v2's orig_lens regeneration pipeline, the Python consumer this CLI replaces CGAL for.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2486  1 LINE
